    "q-110860": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110860",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}c{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$",
      "worked_solution": "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14270355/assets/f60587953ec9bbe05689382b641677058ce8ba070917db340a0ba793170d0951.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}c{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}c{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{c{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9c{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9c{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =[3c{x}^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n3c=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
