    "q-110868": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110868",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & 0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$",
      "worked_solution": "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14270355/assets/a49e679b3919594edc7fe963190a754324b9b5ea980d1936121c040d0ee52284.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nW\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+c\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(c\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[c\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{c\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )}{2} \\\\  & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
