    "q-111164": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111164",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y<2X-2{X}^{2}).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,1]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A=\\{Y<2X-2{X}^{2}\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14270355/assets/bb3b94fbd5ae245b60fbd496be1a4609742bb1958148faeae57ca3ef4054f6da.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<2X-2{X}^{2}) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x-2{x}^{2}}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2x-2{x}^{2}}4xy\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[2x{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=2x-2{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2x(2x-2{x}^{2})^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(8{x}^{3}-16{x}^{4}+8{x}^{5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{4}-\\frac{16{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{4{x}^{6}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{16}{5}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
