    "q-111150": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111150",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{xy}{4},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,2],$ and the event $A=\\{X<Y\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14270355/assets/9213a4b132f625677fcc5719e71900d037ac08088dc477f8d6a93f9ca67bc3d4.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{xy}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{xy}{4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{8}]}_{x=0}^{x=y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{32}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
