    "q-110369": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110369",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>Y).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,1]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A=\\{X>Y\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14270355/assets/023e458b0d61dbb9b4bd475618db63c565abf3cf15bcb7cfc3afd52217b66426.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>Y) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
